      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Multifactor discriminant analysis was used on a computer to examine 100 patients with myocardial infarction in the subacute period (at week 4 of the disease onset) and 76 in the postinfarction period (at months 2-120 of postinfarction). A complex of clinical and coronary signs was defined, which differentiated patients with subacute myocardial infarction and postinfarct cardiosclerosis, as well as those with postinfarct stable and progressive angina pectoris."},
